1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,098
Complex decisions rarely fail because we need one more list of ideas.

2
00:00:06,098 --> 00:00:14,229
The real problem is that goals, constraints, research, trade-offs and next steps are scattered across tabs.

3
00:00:14,229 --> 00:00:20,835
Avenli turns that work into one saved, reviewable path from problem to action.

4
00:00:20,835 --> 00:00:29,474
I describe the outcome I need, the deadline, hard constraints and anything I still do not know.

5
00:00:29,474 --> 00:00:36,588
Avenli saves the problem, then runs a finite workflow instead of an open-ended chat.

6
00:00:36,588 --> 00:00:45,227
This public demo uses fictional data and makes no external calls, while signed-in workspaces persist real analyses.

7
00:00:45,227 --> 00:00:51,833
Eight specialized stages run on NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super through Nebius Token Factory.

8
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:53,866
Intake structures the request.

9
00:00:53,866 --> 00:00:58,439
Planning identifies dependencies and the most important research questions.

10
00:00:58,439 --> 00:01:10,635
Research, verification, option generation, critique, decision and task planning each return typed output that must pass strict validation before the next stage can begin.

11
00:01:10,635 --> 00:01:16,225
For live analyses, Tavily supplies a bounded set of search results.

12
00:01:16,225 --> 00:01:26,389
Avenli assigns its own source IDs, keeps retrieved text outside system instructions and requires exact supporting excerpts for verified claims.

13
00:01:26,389 --> 00:01:31,470
Here I can inspect the sources, publication uncertainty and coverage.

14
00:01:31,470 --> 00:01:36,552
If the evidence is missing, stale or contradictory, confidence drops.

15
00:01:36,552 --> 00:01:44,175
If no decision-relevant claim has a traceable excerpt, Avenli abstains instead of selecting an option.

16
00:01:44,175 --> 00:01:52,305
The workflow can pause for a clarification, survive a reload and resume the same saved run.

17
00:01:52,305 --> 00:01:57,387
The Overview keeps the goal, constraints, unknowns and activity visible.

18
00:01:57,387 --> 00:02:01,960
Proposed tasks remain editable and do not execute automatically.

19
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:04,501
Services are optional in Settings.

20
00:02:04,501 --> 00:02:10,599
For Google Calendar, Avenli first shows the exact title, time and description.

21
00:02:10,599 --> 00:02:14,156
Creating the event requires a separate approval.

22
00:02:14,156 --> 00:02:21,271
The write is idempotent, creates no attendees or invitations and leaves an audit record.

23
00:02:21,271 --> 00:02:31,434
The architecture keeps the browser, authenticated server, durable Supabase state, model and research providers, and external writes behind clear boundaries.

24
00:02:31,434 --> 00:02:41,089
Avenli uses open-model reasoning to produce an evidence-aware plan while keeping the person in control of every real-world action.

25
00:02:41,089 --> 00:02:43,122
Give it a problem.

26
00:02:43,122 --> 00:02:44,647
Get it solved.
